/F2 13 Tf (FORTRESS INDUSTRIAL PLANT - ASSET HEALTH REPORT) Tj T* /F1 10 Tf
(DOCUMENT ID: REP-2026-P101-V4) Tj T*
(EQUIPMENT TAG: PUMP P-101 \(PRIMARY FEED WATER BOOSTER\)) Tj T*
(LOCATION: SECTOR 4, TURBINE AUXILIARY BAY) Tj T*
(DATE OF INSPECTION: AUGUST 14, 2026) Tj T*
(LEAD INSPECTOR: MARCUS VANCE \(CERTIFIED ISO 18436-2 CATEGORY III\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
T* /F2 11 Tf (1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY) Tj T* /F1 10 Tf
(A comprehensive condition monitoring and vibration analysis was conducted on Pump P-101 following reports of abnormal acoustic signatures during peak load operations.) Tj T*
(The main issue identified in Pump P-101 is severe mechanical vibration and advanced outer race degradation on the drive-end \(DE\) spherical roller bearing \(SKF 22218 EK\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
T* /F2 11 Tf (2. OPERATIONAL PARAMETERS RECORDED) Tj T* /F1 10 Tf
(- Operating Speed: 2,980 RPM) Tj T*
(- Flow Rate: 420 m3/hr \(Nominal: 450 m3/hr\)) Tj T*
(- Suction Pressure: 3.2 bar) Tj T*
(- Discharge Pressure: 18.6 bar) Tj T*
(- Motor Drive Current: 84.5 Amperes) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
7 0 obj
<< /Length 895 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
14.5 TL
50 750 Td
/F2 13 Tf (PUMP P-101 INSPECTION REPORT \(CONTINUED\) - PAGE 2) Tj T* /F1 10 Tf
(ASSET: P-101 FEED WATER BOOSTER PUMP) Tj T*
() Tj T*
T* /F2 11 Tf (3. VIBRATION ANALYSIS & MEASUREMENTS) Tj T* /F1 10 Tf
(Overall vibration levels were measured using triaxial accelerometers mounted on non-drive-end \(NDE\) and drive-end \(DE\) bearing housings.) Tj T*
(- Measured Overall Vibration Level \(Drive-End Radial\): 7.2 mm/s RMS \(ISO 10816-3 Zone D: Critical/Unacceptable\)) Tj T*
(- Baseline Acceptable Vibration: 1.8 mm/s RMS) Tj T*
(- Peak Acceleration: 4.8 g pk-pk in the 1.2 kHz - 3.5 kHz demodulated frequency spectrum.) Tj T*
(- High amplitude peaks observed at 118.4 Hz matching the Outer Race Ball Pass Frequency \(BPFO\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
T* /F2 11 Tf (4. THERMOGRAPHIC FINDINGS) Tj T* /F1 10 Tf
(- Drive-end bearing housing skin temperature: 88.4 deg C \(Exceeds maximum allowable limit of 70 deg C\).) Tj T*
(- Lubricant oil sample: High iron particulate concentration \(142 ppm\), indicating active metal-to-metal spalling.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
8 0 obj
<< /Length 877 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
14.5 TL
50 750 Td
/F2 13 Tf (PUMP P-101 INSPECTION REPORT \(CONTINUED\) - PAGE 3) Tj T* /F1 10 Tf
(ASSET: P-101 FEED WATER BOOSTER PUMP) Tj T*
() Tj T*
T* /F2 11 Tf (5. ROOT CAUSE ASSESSMENT) Tj T* /F1 10 Tf
(The excessive vibration and thermal runaway are caused by lubrication starvation and contamination, which resulted in micro-spalling of the drive-end bearing raceway.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
T* /F2 11 Tf (6. RECOMMENDED MAINTENANCE ACTIONS) Tj T* /F1 10 Tf
(The following immediate maintenance actions are mandated:) Tj T*
(- Action 1 \(Critical\): Perform an immediate scheduled shutdown of Pump P-101 within 14 days.) Tj T*
(- Action 2: Replace drive-end bearing \(SKF 22218 EK\) and inspect shaft sleeve for fretting corrosion.) Tj T*
(- Action 3: Flush the oil reservoir and replenish with ISO VG 46 synthetic lubricating oil.) Tj T*
(- Action 4: Verify dynamic alignment between motor and pump coupling \(tolerance < 0.05 mm radial runout\).) Tj T*
(- Action 5: Re-commission and perform post-maintenance vibration verification.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(REPORT APPROVED BY:) Tj T*
(H. Thorne, Head of Plant Reliability Engineering) Tj T*
ET
endstream
